Z||000006||skitime||05-25-2001||09:52 PM||||Well, Bruce now that you stopped over at my house, you know you have a local support group.  That is real important because you know you among friends who also Forumoholics. We have meetings nearly every night but seating is limited to whatever you can find in the garage. As you know parking is limited but Fieros get the preferred parking spaces. With your engine knowledge, you have a lot to contribute to our meetings. We need to hear more of your inspiring talks on flowmeters and engine transplants and your spare Quad4 and five speed trans. If you can't make the meetings than you need to contribute on the forum as therapy.  The best cure is buy some additional Fieros so that you can be content when you are not on the forum.  I know that although that has not worked for us yet it is perhaps because we haven't purchased enough cars yet. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-008f.jpg"> <BR>You might find it useful to add to you computer setup so that it might not be so obvious that you have an addiction problem. I set myself up in a little corner out of the way where no one will notice what I am doing. I also networked computers into each of my two daughters rooms so they do bother me to get off the computer.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P5250015.jpg"> <BR>Good luck we will be here for you when you  fall off the wagon.<P>Dave<BR>||||reg||1
