Z||000015||Brucepts||05-26-2001||10:25 PM||||Wouldn't say hardcore just yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I've had my 84 SE for the last 10 years it has sat idle for the past 2. I got it back on the road last week and found this forum and its wealth of knowledge! Skitime is maybe 10min drive from me. I've been playing with Garden tractor pulling for the past few years building my own motors and tractors. I have a shop (well my wife's side of the garage) full of equipment, mill, lathe and my own flowbench. I'd like to find an old 2.8 stick and make myself a "junkyard" hotrod. I have lots of ideas but lack of cash is my problem. The neat thing about this car is all the parts that fit out of other cars so junkyard surfin is a great place to build performance. I like the idea of a 3.4 with some serious flow work on a set of heads/intake sitting in that engine bay. <P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .||||reg||1
